    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] 2026-11-01 review: ir.py:393-396 and to_dict still emit files_skipped as an int on every run. Since 6e7e48bf42 (INV-virik), failed_files and warnings are emitted only when non-empty, so the 'failed_files=[] and warnings=[] on all runs' wording is stale. On the packages/ self-analysis, 99/99 ARs have an int files_skipped and 2 have a failed_files list. The type asymmetry remains, now with presence asymmetry on top. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nOn all 84 AnalysisRuns, the three parallel 'what didn't go right this pass' fields use two container types: files_skipped=0 (int) while failed_files=[] and warnings=[] (lists). A consumer iterating the per-pass problem channels must special-case files_skipped. Fix: harmonize the AR what-went-wrong field container types (e.g. make files_skipped a list, or document the intentional asymmetry). Distinct from INV-buhur (satisfied: failed_files never populated) — different mechanism. Surfaced via dogfooding; blinded severity 2/5."  # 7de0
